   "_id": 12536,
   "ANSWER": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1115\" data-start=\"1000\">Disk attachment refers to how secondary storage (disks) are connected to the system.<br data-end=\"1103\" data-start=\"1100\" />\nTwo types:</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1192\" data-start=\"1119\"><strong data-end=\"1144\" data-start=\"1119\">Host-Attached Storage</strong> &ndash; connected directly to computer (e.g., SATA)</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1255\" data-start=\"1196\"><strong data-end=\"1230\" data-start=\"1196\">Network-Attached Storage (NAS)</strong> &ndash; accessed via a network</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1629\" data-start=\"1551\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1282\" data-start=\"1257\"><strong data-end=\"1280\" data-start=\"1260\">Mark Allocation:</strong></p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1303\" data-start=\"1285\">Definition &ndash; 40%</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1335\" data-start=\"1306\">Any two correct types &ndash; 60%</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1382\" data-start=\"1338\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
